WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.630
Jewish law forbids eating pork.

2
00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:06.870
So can a Jewish heart patient
accept a valve taken from a pig?

3
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.090
And may a Jewish scientist
test a new cancer drug on mice?

4
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.150
The Torah and Talmud were written
long before hospitals and labs.

5
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.750
So how can they guide Jews on
cloning, euthanasia and gender?

6
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.600
In this mission, you'll trace
how Jewish sources value life,

7
00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.560
from before birth to
the last days of life.

8
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.590
Then you'll compare how Orthodox, Masorti
and Reform Jews answer questions about

9
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.640
sexuality and gender.

10
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.710
Your mission: find out how laws written
long before hospitals and labs can guide

11
00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.810
Jews today.
